# Database migrations

Revision files are in `versions/`. Run Alembic from the `backend` directory so it can load `main.py` and the application models.

After changing a model, generate a revision and read through it before applying it:

```powershell
python -m alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe the change"
python -m alembic upgrade head
```

Set `DATABASE_URL` before running these commands against PostgreSQL. Local development uses `brightloop.db` by default. Vercel checks the recorded revision at startup and won’t serve the API until the database is up to date.
